SUMMARY:Angel Island Hike | 6 miles  (Leave on Tiburon Ferry at 10:00)
DESCRIPTION:Mindfull Hikes\n**\\*\\*\\*\\* Registration is closed (6/26/20
 26)\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\nThis hike is for members who have attended two or
  more hikes in the last three months and buy a ferry ticket. Everyone will
  start off on the waitlist. ***When you buy your ticket let me know and I'
 ll move you to 'going'.*** Group size is limited.\n\n***Please be in good 
 enough shape to hike at a moderate/fast steady pace (+/-2.5 mph) and comfo
 rtable with elevation changes.***\n\n**Distance:** +/- 6.2 miles total\n**
 The hike:** Venturing out from our usual hiking places to have a little fu
 n. A loop hike along north ridge trail\, ida trail\, fire road and sunset 
 trail. Exquisite views along the way from multiple perspectives.\n\nWe'll 
 take the 10:00 AM ferry from Tiburon to Angel Island\, hike and return on 
 the 2:20 or 3:20 PM ferry from Angel Island to Tiburon.\n\n**Where to Meet
 :** Caffè Acri in Tiburon at 9:27 AM\n\n**Link to buy your ferry ticket:*
 * https://angelislandferry.com/schedule/\n\n**What to bring:** Lunch\, wat
 er\, hat\, good hiking shoes\, a joyful spirit and laughter. Please dress 
 appropriately for the weather that day. Layers of clothing are always advi
 sable.\n**===================================**\n**Reminders:**\nMindful h
 ikes are intended to be a way to connect more fully with ourselves\, each 
 other and with the land. There will be two periods of silent walking throu
 ghout the hike to allow the senses to be fully alive and felt. There will 
 also be time during the hike to visit and connect with each other. These t
 imes of talking and connecting are an invitation to bring mindfulness to t
 he present moment. **It's a time to put away the cell phone and cameras to
  disengage from technology to be fully present with each other\, our *sens
 es and the land we are inhabiting.***\n\n**Dāna**\nIn the spirit of the B
 uddhist tradition mindful hikes are offered as a dāna based event. Rick H
 ansen says “generosity is a beautiful practice that opens and gladdens t
 he heart\, relaxes the contraction of ‘self’ and ripples out into the 
 world to touch many people.” The dāna practice is **heart centered** an
 d in the spirit of generosity. Venmo or cash is graciously accepted. Venmo
  account is: @vickieix8\; last four digits 4714 of my phone # if asked.
